[Enjin patch] LLGI Vulkan: only colour attachment 0 is written
================================================================
The engine's main pass has two colour attachments (colour + velocity).
LLGI's Vulkan pipeline gives every attachment a full RGBA write mask, while
Effekseer's fragment shaders write output 0 only, so attachment 1 would
receive undefined values. This patch gives attachments past the first a write
mask of zero and leaves their blend state at its default.

Against LLGI 8c476bdea911d99dc307655be3cad1cc2b8d5a1e (the submodule commit of
Effekseer tag 1807). The file lives at
third_party/effekseer/3rdParty/LLGI/src/Vulkan/LLGI.PipelineStateVulkan.cpp.
--- a/src/Vulkan/LLGI.PipelineStateVulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/Vulkan/LLGI.PipelineStateVulkan.cpp
@@ -382,6 +382,15 @@
 		blendInfo.colorWriteMask = vk::ColorComponentFlagBits::eR | vk::ColorComponentFlagBits::eG | vk::ColorComponentFlagBits::eB |
 								   vk::ColorComponentFlagBits::eA;
 
+		// [Enjin patch] Effekseer shaders write colour output 0 only. The engine's
+		// main pass has a second attachment (velocity); leave every attachment
+		// past the first untouched instead of writing undefined values into it.
+		if (i > 0)
+		{
+			blendInfo.colorWriteMask = vk::ColorComponentFlags();
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		if (IsBlendEnabled)
 		{
 			blendInfo.blendEnable = true;
